Z||000000||DrRodey||05-13-2001||05:43 PM||||heres the story.....   replaced plugs, wires, and fuel filter last week, this morning I get six blocks from my house and it kills.. acts like it isn't getting fuel.  I re-start it, idles fine, ****  into first let out the clutch it starts dying again push in the clutch and it is fine again.. . To get the damn thing to move i have to Rev it to 2500 and drop the clutch and then i have to pray that i'm lucky cause that doen't always work??  any ideas.. i'm completely cerfuddeled on this one..??<P>Thanks.<P>Dan.<P><BR>oh by the way... 84, duke four speed nasscar centerforce clutch 163k(on engine and tranny  5k on clutch)||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||05-13-2001||05:53 PM||||Have you checked the MAP sensor?<P>I can mail you a good one if you want to try it out. Would take a few days to get to you though.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 05-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DrRodey||05-13-2001||07:21 PM||||How would I go about checking the MAP sensor???  I have checked the computer for codes and it gives me a 13 and sometimes a 24.  Would that be it.??||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GTZ34||05-14-2001||01:31 AM||||DR - Code 24 is  VSS setting.  My 87 manual says code 24 will set if VSS reads 0 mph and RPMs rev between 1400 & 3600 which is where 2500 is, TPS &lt; 2% hmmm, low load, not in park or neutral, and all this happens for 5 seconds.  A code 13 is an O2 setting.<P>When I get codes, I always disconnect the batt (for at leasst 10 sec) and let them set again to verify the code set conditions.<P>Hope this helps. GL||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||05-14-2001||08:36 AM||||when a car idles but wont take a load that is one sign of a bad distributor cap and rotor - its possible your new plugs and wires increased the amount of spark you were getting through the cap, and if it was arcing inside the cap the increase could have 'finished it off'<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||PAUL88GT||05-14-2001||03:35 PM||||My guess is the pick-up coil on the distributor.  Mine was falling apart and I had similar symptoms.  You will have to pull the distributor to replace it.  Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DrRodey||05-14-2001||10:30 PM||||ok here's how the story ends... took me all d*** day but i finally got her runnin good again.. replaced O2, entire distributer, regaped plugs, and while doin that i bumped the pos. cable from the battery sending sparks flying everywhere..... all that work and it was just a friggin melted battery wire that was grounding out....   Oh well.. with all that new stuff she purrs again...<P>thanks for all the help.<P><BR>Dan<P>DrRodey||||reg||1
